### PINN benchmark [kdv] KdV: u = sech^2(0.5(x-t)), x in [-8,8], t in [0,2]
## Optimizer comparison, third member: the extended Kalman filter.
## bench/opt_simple, bench/opt_ngd and bench/opt_kalman are the same
## problem, data, network and seed; only the method and the epoch budget
## differ.  The residual is nonlinear (A u u_x), which is the case the
## filter observes through kf_update_resid rather than as a linear
## functional of the carried derivatives.
## GD_param: p1 = initial covariance diagonal, p2 = initial forgetting
## factor, p3 = its schedule.
Rand_seed    20260728 / fixed seed (reproducibility)
Output_deriv 1 /
Init_w       LeCun_unif
Restart      0 /
Nlayer       4 / L
2 /
16 /
16 /
1 /
###
Loss_term  DATA         100  data.dat           1.d0 /
Loss_term  COLLOCATION     200  colloc.dat         0.2d0 /
###
Residual 3 /
LIN   1.d0        0 1 /  u_t
UUX   3.d0        1 0 /  A u u_x (A=3)
LIN   1.d0        3 0 /  u_3x
Exact_solution 1 /
Hod_check 1 /
###
Num_validation 30 /
Validation_cyc 100 /
P_max          1000000 /
###
Epoch      1000 /
Activation TANH /
Conv       1.d-14 /
Num_batch  270 /
Checkpoint_cyc         100000 /
GD_method  KALMAN
GD_param   1.d-3 0.995d0 0.9999d0 0.d0 0.d0 /
